{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1523760-storypath-police-interrogation-scenes","id":1523760,"title":"[Storypath] 'Police Interrogation' scenes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-07T02:02:38-07:00","id":1523760,"title":"[Storypath] 'Police Interrogation' scenes","content":"I'm preparing <i><b>'Police Interrogation'</b></i> Scene in <b>Trinity Aeon era</b>. Like the one from <b>TC Core</b> chapter cover image - only in 2120 year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img width=\"551\" height=\"788\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/lEtIYJ2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/lEtIYJ2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/lEtIYJ2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I suppose I run 'Police Interrogation' as Intrigue mechanics? <i><b>Suspect</b></i> is <b>corporation ex-special forces security</b>. <i><b>Integrators </b></i>are PCs, with Lunar police detective leading it.<br /> <br /> As I understand, mechanics for scene like this looks like this...<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i><b>Suspect</b></i> has <b>Attitude</b> to PCs as <b>3 = Enemy</b> - They contained him and handcuffed, he is arrested because of them.</li> <li>Convincing <i><b>Suspect</b></i> to say incriminating Higgins - or better, point his higher-ups would be then <b>Influence</b> action?</li> <li>Get to confession would then be some simple <b>Persuasion + Manipulation</b> roll? <b>Complex</b> action with some <b>Milestones</b>? ( Like maybe <b>Composure</b> dots of <i><b>Suspect</b></i> ?)\u200b\u200b\u200b</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T04:28:21-07:00","id":1523767,"title":"","content":"Interrogation is actually a cross between Intrigue and Procedural. Intrigue to convince and Procedural to gather information and process it.<br /> <br /> You have 2 approaches in a interrogation, Good Cop and Bad Cop.<br /> Good Cop try to improve the attitude to make it easier to convince the target to speak.<br /> Bad Cop try to stress the target so much that the target lose control and talk.<br /> The interaction of the 2 is good too, with the bad cop stressing the target, it becomes far easier to seam the good cop is really good.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend House Rules: Mental and Social, as there are a bunch of stunts to use, make it more flexible than a few rolls with simples result.<br /> Also the rules for Stress and Trauma in House Rules The Basics are a good option for you in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T14:38:43-07:00","id":1523782,"title":"","content":"Agreed that it would be an Influence action to get someone to talk and then Information Gathering to gather useful information, at least if you're working with a hostile suspect or witness who has useful information. If you just want to get a full confession I think it would just be an Influence action.<br /> <br /> Influence/Information Gathering would be good to represent an interview where you're getting information and finding inconsistencies and lies that can be used later in court (or maybe as Enhancement to get a full confession later). This can be a fun way of letting your players sort of assemble the pieces of the puzzle.<br /> <br /> If they've already done all of the investigation and you really just want to get the guilty party to admit it, I'd probably suggest just doing Influence. Depending on how big of a set piece you want the interrogation to be, I'd either treat it as a simple Encourage Behavior influence action, or a complex action with multiple milestones if you want to spend awhile breaking the suspect down.<br /> <br /> For a simple one, you could just use the base difficulty of the target's resolve (or since they are probably an Antagonist I'd use their Desperation Pool) as the Difficulty, then increase the Difficulty by the negative attitude. That probably results in an unreasonably high diff, at which point the players will probably need to make a few attempts to Shift Attitude first. In a situation like this you'll probably get the confession after a few rolls and you can move on.<br /> <br /> For a complex action you could set a max number of attempts and the time each roll takes in such a way as to describe how long before the cops have to let the suspect go. Maybe it is 3 milestones, but they have 5 max rolls (or more if you have multiple players who will want to really engage with this). If they've already done a bunch of investigating I'd let them cash in clues they've gathered for enhancement, representing them questioning the suspect about specific things. If you want a more dynamic scene I'd make the difficulty Opposed, so the suspect rolls one of their dicepools to set the difficulty for each roll. For teamwork I really like how Storypath Ultra handles it, all of the players participating in the roll have to roll the exact same dice pool, then they pool their successes (or hits) to buy off the difficulty and purchase stunts. If you have characters who aren't that social they could be monitoring the interrogation via AR or something, and have them use Information Gathering to get additional clues they can feed back to the interrogators (perhaps they're pulling up camera feeds to double check the alibi of the suspect, or they notice heart rate changes from sensors in the room indicating the suspect lied about something). To represent good cop/bad cop you could have two players doing the interrogation generating enhancement for each other.<br /> <br /> It does feel weird that the Intrigue systems doesn't have a good way to model sort of negative influence, where you are hostile to a target to intimidate them into doing something. If you have players who'll want to do that, I'd def check out Mateus' house rules since that will provide more satisfying options than just &quot;I roll Persuasion + Strength to punch the table and say something mean, and generate enhancement for the good cop to actually use the Intrigue rules.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T03:07:00-07:00","id":1523907,"title":"","content":"A few tips from movies and TV on how to conduct Interogations - j <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DgU-q384pO4?si=zsPBm589L1nE5Wpj\" data-code=\"DgU-q384pO4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DgU-q384pO4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}